1. while loop: 
A while loop will continuously execute code depending on the value of a condition. It begins with the keyword while, followed by a comparison to be evaluated, then a colon. 
On the next line is the code block to be executed, indented to the right. Similar to an if statement, the code in the body will only be executed if the comparison is evaluated to be true. What sets a while loop apart, however,
is that this code block will keep executing as long as the evaluation statement is true. Once the statement is no longer true, the loop exits and the next line of code will be executed.  

while loops
A while loop executes the body of the loop while a specified condition remains True. They are commonly used when there’s an unknown number of operations to be performed, and a condition needs to be checked at each iteration.

syntax: 
while specified condition is True:
    body of loop 

basic example: 
-------
my_variable = 5
while my_variable < 10:
    print("Hello")
    my_variable += 1

